# Strawberry Fields Forever, intro (figure 105.1): chords over the mellotron's bottom line.
# The bracketed (a) is the a-minor chord Pollack hears implied in the second half of bar 1. The last
# bar has two extra beats (essay), so it is six beats long; the E-flat over the held B-flat bass is
# the "forced 6/4 -> 5/3 plagal cadence".
#? Octave of the bottom line (F3 down to Bb2) is chosen for range.
key B-flat

system
chords "Chords"   | F{V} (a) | c{ii} A-dim{vii-dim} | B-flat{I} F{V} | <6> E-flat{IV} B-flat{I} |
bass "Bottom"     | F3 E3 | Eb3 | D3 C3 | <6> Bb2 |
